{"id":"4c768bbe33419a36e270fd27751f5b50e438f2e5","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"4c768bbe33419a36e270fd27751f5b50e438f2e5","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"man/systemd-analyze.xml","lines":["@@ -184,6 +184,12 @@","       <arg choice=\"plain\">fdstore</arg>","       <arg choice=\"plain\" rep=\"repeat\"><replaceable>UNIT</replaceable></arg>","     </cmdsynopsis>","+    <cmdsynopsis>","+      <command>systemd-analyze</command>","+      <arg choice=\"opt\" rep=\"repeat\">OPTIONS</arg>","+      <arg choice=\"plain\">restart-delays</arg>","+      <arg choice=\"plain\" rep=\"repeat\"><replaceable>SERVICE</replaceable></arg>","+    </cmdsynopsis>","     <cmdsynopsis>","       <command>systemd-analyze</command>","       <arg choice=\"opt\" rep=\"repeat\">OPTIONS</arg>","@@ -981,6 +987,54 @@ stored sock 0:8   4213190 -      socket:[4213190] ro","       \"DEVNO\".</para>","     </refsect2>"," ","+    <refsect2>","+      <title><command>systemd-analyze restart-delays <replaceable>SERVICE</replaceable>…</command></title>","+","+      <para>Shows how long the service manager waits before each automatic restart of the specified service","+      units, as configured with <varname>RestartSec=</varname>, <varname>RestartSteps=</varname>, and","+      <varname>RestartMaxDelaySec=</varname>, see","+      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.service</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>.","+      The table lists each restart until the delay stops growing, with its delay and the total of the delays","+      up to that restart. Below the table, <command>systemd-analyze</command> shows whether the start rate","+      limit configured with <varname>StartLimitIntervalSec=</varname> and <varname>StartLimitBurst=</varname>","+      rejects a restart, and when, see","+      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.unit</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>. If","+      the start rate limit rejects a restart that is listed in the table, the table ends with that","+      restart.</para>","+","+      <para>The times do not include the time the service takes to start, run, and stop, or the delay added","+      by <varname>RestartRandomizedDelaySec=</varname>. They assume that the restart counter is 0 at the","+      first start, and that no earlier start counts against the start rate limit. Any start other than an","+      automatic restart resets the restart counter, unless the unit is waiting for an automatic restart at","+      that point. <command>systemctl reset-failed</command> resets the restart counter and start rate","+      limit.</para>","+","+      <para>With <option>--offline=yes</option>, the arguments are unit files, which","+      <command>systemd-analyze</command> loads together with their drop-ins. Settings that neither the unit","+      files nor their drop-ins set use their built-in defaults, and <command>systemd-analyze</command>","+      ignores","+      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-system.conf</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>","+","+      <para><command>systemd-analyze</command> refuses to show a unit with exponential backoff and a","+      <varname>RestartSteps=</varname> value above 10000.</para>","+","+      <example>","+        <title>Restart delays of a service</title>","+","+        <programlisting>$ systemd-analyze restart-delays example.service","+RESTART    DELAY    TOTAL","+      1      10s      10s","+      2      20s      30s","+      3      40s 1min 10s","+      4 1min 20s 2min 30s","+      5 2min 40s 5min 10s","+","+The start limit rejects restart 5, 5min 10s after the first start, and example.service enters the failed state.</programlisting>","+      </example>","+","+      <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v263\"/>","+    </refsect2>","+","     <refsect2>","       <title><command>systemd-analyze image-policy <replaceable>POLICY</replaceable>…</command></title>"," ","@@ -1424,7 +1478,8 @@ boot  efi  exitrd  init  lib32\tlibx32\tmedia\t    opt  root  sbin  sys  usr  vmlin","           <para>Specifies fallback instance name for template units. This will be used when one or more","           template units without an instance name (e.g. <filename>foo@.service</filename>) specified for","           <command>systemd-analyze condition</command> with <option>--unit=</option>,","-          <command>systemd-analyze security</command>, and <command>systemd-analyze verify</command>.","+          <command>systemd-analyze restart-delays</command>, <command>systemd-analyze security</command>,","+          and <command>systemd-analyze verify</command>.","           If unspecified, <literal>test_instance</literal> will be used.</para>"," ","           <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v257\"/>","@@ -1451,9 +1506,9 @@ boot  efi  exitrd  init  lib32\tlibx32\tmedia\t    opt  root  sbin  sys  usr  vmlin","         <term><option>--root=<replaceable>PATH</replaceable></option></term>"," ","         <listitem><para>With <command>cat-config</command>, <command>verify</command>,","-        <command>condition</command>, <command>unit-gdb</command>, and <command>security</command> when","-        used with <option>--offline=</option>, operate on files underneath the specified root path","-        <replaceable>PATH</replaceable>.</para>","+        <command>condition</command>, <command>unit-gdb</command>, and with <command>security</command> and","+        <command>restart-delays</command> when used with <option>--offline=</option>, operate on files","+        underneath the specified root path <replaceable>PATH</replaceable>.</para>"," ","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v239\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>","@@ -1462,9 +1517,9 @@ boot  efi  exitrd  init  lib32\tlibx32\tmedia\t    opt  root  sbin  sys  usr  vmlin","         <term><option>--image=<replaceable>PATH</replaceable></option></term>"," ","         <listitem><para>With <command>cat-config</command>, <command>verify</command>,","-        <command>condition</command> and <command>security</command> when used with","-        <option>--offline=</option>, operate on files inside the specified image path","-        <replaceable>PATH</replaceable>.</para>","+        <command>condition</command>, and with <command>security</command> and","+        <command>restart-delays</command> when used with <option>--offline=</option>, operate on files","+        inside the specified image path <replaceable>PATH</replaceable>.</para>"," ","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v250\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>","@@ -1482,6 +1537,10 @@ boot  efi  exitrd  init  lib32\tlibx32\tmedia\t    opt  root  sbin  sys  usr  vmlin","         <option>--threshold=</option> (default value is 100), <option>--offline=</option> will return","         an error.</para>"," ","+        <para>With <command>restart-delays</command>, load the specified unit files instead of asking the","+        service manager for the settings of loaded units. <option>--offline=</option> can be used with","+        <option>--root=</option> and <option>--image=</option> here too.</para>","+","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v250\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>"," ","@@ -1800,6 +1859,16 @@ boot  efi  exitrd  init  lib32\tlibx32\tmedia\t    opt  root  sbin  sys  usr  vmlin","         that the service was initially told to deactivate.","         </para>"," ","+        <para>With the <command>restart-delays</command> command, generate a JSON object for each unit with","+        the following fields: <varname>unit</varname> which is the unit name, <varname>restarts</varname>","+        which is an array with the <varname>restart</varname> number, the <varname>delayUSec</varname> and","+        the <varname>totalUSec</varname> of each row of the table, <varname>furtherDelayUSec</varname> which","+        is the delay of every further restart, and <varname>startLimitHitRestart</varname> and","+        <varname>startLimitHitUSec</varname> which are the number and time of the restart that the start rate","+        limit rejects. The start rate limit fields are omitted if the start rate limit never rejects a","+        restart. If the service manager never restarts the unit, <varname>restarts</varname> is empty and","+        the other fields are omitted.</para>","+","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v250\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>"," ","@@ -1855,6 +1924,10 @@ boot  efi  exitrd  init  lib32\tlibx32\tmedia\t    opt  root  sbin  sys  usr  vmlin","         <option>--table</option> or <option>--json=</option>, no legends or hints are included in the output.","         </para>"," ","+        <para>When used with the <command>restart-delays</command> command, suppress the","+        <literal>RESTART</literal>, <literal>DELAY</literal>, and <literal>TOTAL</literal> column headers","+        of the restart delay table.</para>","+","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v253\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>"," "],"additions":80,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"man/systemd.service.xml","lines":["@@ -656,6 +656,10 @@ RestartMaxDelaySec=160s</programlisting>","         in the same format as <varname>RestartSec=</varname>, or <literal>infinity</literal>","         to disable the setting. Defaults to <literal>infinity</literal>.</para>"," ","+        <para><command>systemd-analyze restart-delays</command> shows the delays of a service and whether the","+        start rate limit stops its restarts, see","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-analyze</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>","+","         <para>This setting is effective only if <varname>RestartSteps=</varname> is also set and","         <varname>RestartSec=</varname> is not zero.</para>"," "],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"shell-completion/bash/systemd-analyze","lines":["@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@ _systemd_analyze() {","         [ARCHITECTURES]='architectures'","         [CPU_FEATURES]='cpu-features'","         [FDSTORE]='fdstore'","+        [RESTART_DELAYS]='restart-delays'","         [CAPABILITY]='capability'","         [TRANSIENT_SETTINGS]='transient-settings'","         [UNIT_SHELL]='unit-shell'","@@ -269,6 +270,16 @@ _systemd_analyze() {","             comps=$( __get_services $mode )","         fi"," ","+    elif __contains_word \"$verb\" ${VERBS[RESTART_DELAYS]}; then","+        if [[ $cur = -* ]]; then","+            comps='--help --version --system --user -H --host -M --machine --no-pager --no-legend --json=off --json=pretty --json=short --offline --root --image --instance --generators'","+        elif ! __contains_word \"--offline\" ${COMP_WORDS[*]}; then","+            comps=$( __get_services $mode )","+        else","+            comps=$( compgen -A file -- \"$cur\" )","+            compopt -o filenames","+        fi","+","     elif __contains_word \"$verb\" ${VERBS[CAPABILITY]}; then","         if [[ $cur = -* ]]; then","             comps='--help --version --no-pager --json=off --json=pretty --json=short -m --mask'"],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"shell-completion/zsh/_systemd-analyze","lines":["@@ -31,6 +31,11 @@","         _sd_unit_files","     }"," ","+(( $+functions[_systemd-analyze_restart-delays] )) ||","+    _systemd-analyze_restart-delays() {","+        _sd_unit_files","+    }","+"," (( $+functions[_systemd-analyze_syscall-filter] )) ||","     _systemd-analyze_syscall-filter() {","         local -a _groups","@@ -97,6 +102,7 @@","             'timestamp:Parse a systemd syntax timestamp'","             'timespan:Parse a systemd syntax timespan'","             'security:Analyze security settings of a service'","+            'restart-delays:Show restart delays and start limit of a service'","             'inspect-elf:Parse and print ELF package metadata'","             'dlopen-metadata:Parse and print ELF dlopen metadata'","             'has-tpm2:Report whether TPM2 support is available'","@@ -138,7 +144,7 @@ _arguments \\","     '--root=[Add support for root argument]:PATH' \\","     '--image=[Add support for discrete images]:PATH' \\","     '--recursive-errors=[When verifying a unit, control dependency verification]:MODE' \\","-    '--offline=[Perform a security review of the specified unit files]:BOOL:(yes no)' \\","+    '--offline=[Analyze the specified unit files instead of loaded units]:BOOL:(yes no)' \\","     '--threshold=[Set a value to compare the overall security exposure level with]: NUMBER' \\","     '--security-policy=[Use customized requirements to compare unit files against]: PATH' \\","     \"--json=[Generate a JSON output of the security analysis table or plot's raw time data]:MODE:(pretty short off)\" \\"],"additions":7,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/analyze/analyze-restart-delays.c","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,420 @@","+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later */","+","+#include \"sd-bus.h\"","+#include \"sd-json.h\"","+","+#include \"alloc-util.h\"","+#include \"analyze.h\"","+#include \"analyze-restart-delays.h\"","+#include \"analyze-verify-util.h\"","+#include \"bus-error.h\"","+#include \"bus-map-properties.h\"","+#include \"bus-util.h\"","+#include \"exit-status.h\"","+#include \"format-table.h\"","+#include \"json-util.h\"","+#include \"manager.h\"","+#include \"pager.h\"","+#include \"ratelimit.h\"","+#include \"service.h\"","+#include \"string-util.h\"","+#include \"strv.h\"","+#include \"time-util.h\"","+#include \"unit-name.h\"","+","+/* The table has a row for each step, and start_limit_hit() checks the start limit once for each step. With","+ * RestartSteps= close to UINT_MAX, the table grows until memory runs out. */","+#define RESTART_STEPS_MAX 10000U","+","+typedef struct RestartSettings {","+        char *id;","+        char *load_state;","+        char *restart;","+        bool restart_forced;","+        usec_t restart_usec;","+        unsigned restart_steps;","+        usec_t restart_max_delay_usec;","+        usec_t start_limit_interval_usec;","+        unsigned start_limit_burst;","+} RestartSettings;","+","+static void restart_settings_done(RestartSettings *rs) {","+        assert(rs);","+","+        rs->id = mfree(rs->id);","+        rs->load_state = mfree(rs->load_state);","+        rs->restart = mfree(rs->restart);","+}","+","+static usec_t restart_delay(const RestartSettings *rs, unsigned n) {","+        assert(rs);","+","+        return service_restart_usec_nth(rs->restart_usec, rs->restart_max_delay_usec, rs->restart_steps, n);","+}","+","+/* Returns the number of the restart after which every restart waits the same delay. */","+static unsigned restart_growth(const RestartSettings *rs) {","+        assert(rs);","+","+        if (!service_restart_backoff_enabled(rs->restart_usec, rs->restart_max_delay_usec, rs->restart_steps))","+                return 1;","+","+        assert(rs->restart_steps <= RESTART_STEPS_MAX);","+        return rs->restart_steps + 1;","+}","+","+/* Returns the number of the restart that the start limit rejects, or 0 if the start limit never rejects a","+ * restart. The time of the rejected restart is relative to the first start of the unit. */","+static uint64_t start_limit_hit(const RestartSettings *rs, usec_t *ret_usec) {","+        assert(rs);","+        assert(ret_usec);","+","+        *ret_usec = USEC_INFINITY;","+","+        RateLimit rl = {","+                .interval = rs->start_limit_interval_usec,","+                .burst = rs->start_limit_burst,","+        };","+","+        if (!ratelimit_configured(&rl))","+                return 0;","+","+        /* ratelimit_below_at() treats a window that begins at 0 as unset, so let's start the clock at 1. The","+         * service manager checks the start limit for the first start of the unit too. */","+        usec_t ts = 1;","+        assert_se(ratelimit_below_at(&rl, ts));","+","+        unsigned growth = restart_growth(rs);","+        for (unsigned n = 1; n <= growth; n++) {","+                ts = usec_add(ts, restart_delay(rs, n));","+                if (!ratelimit_below_at(&rl, ts)) {","+                        *ret_usec = ts - 1;","+                        return n;","+                }","+        }","+","+        /* Every further restart waits d, and no earlier restart waited longer than d. If","+         * StartLimitIntervalSec= is at least StartLimitBurst= times d, the current window of the start limit","+         * contains the restart that the start limit rejects. If StartLimitIntervalSec= is shorter, no","+         * window contains more than StartLimitBurst= restarts that are d apart, and the start limit never","+         * rejects a restart. */","+        usec_t d = restart_delay(rs, growth + 1);","+        usec_t end = ratelimit_end(&rl);","+        uint64_t in_window = d == 0 || end == USEC_INFINITY ? UINT64_MAX : (end - ts) / d;","+        uint64_t left = rl.burst - rl.num;","+        if (in_window <= left)","+                return 0;","+","+        usec_t p;","+        *ret_usec = MUL_SAFE(&p, left + 1, d) ? usec_add(ts, p) - 1 : USEC_INFINITY;","+        return growth + left + 1;","+}","+","+static int show_never_restarted(const RestartSettings *rs, const char *setting) {","+        _cleanup_(sd_json_variant_unrefp) sd_json_variant *v = NULL;","+        int r;","+","+        assert(rs);","+        assert(setting);","+","+        if (!sd_json_format_enabled(arg_json_format_flags)) {","+                printf(\"%s has %s, so the service manager never restarts it.\\n\", rs->id, setting);","+                return 0;","+        }","+","+        r = sd_json_buildo(","+                        &v,","+                        SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_STRING(\"unit\", rs->id),","+                        SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR(\"restarts\", SD_JSON_BUILD_EMPTY_ARRAY));","+        if (r < 0)","+                return log_oom();","+","+        return sd_json_variant_dump(v, arg_json_format_flags, stdout, NULL);","+}","+","+static int show_restart_delays(const RestartSettings *rs, bool *printed) {","+        _cleanup_(sd_json_variant_unrefp) sd_json_variant *v = NULL, *jrestarts = NULL;","+        _cleanup_(table_unrefp) Table *table = NULL;","+        const char *never_restarted = NULL;","+        usec_t total = 0, hit_usec;","+        uint64_t hit;","+        int r;","+","+        assert(rs);","+        assert(printed);","+","+        /* The service manager never arms the restart timer for an infinite delay. */","+        if (rs->restart_usec == USEC_INFINITY)","+                never_restarted = \"RestartSec=infinity\";","+        else if (streq_ptr(rs->restart, \"no\") && !rs->restart_forced)","+                never_restarted = \"Restart=no\";","+","+        if (!never_restarted && rs->restart_steps > RESTART_STEPS_MAX &&","+            service_restart_backoff_enabled(rs->restart_usec, rs->restart_max_delay_usec, rs->restart_steps))","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(E2BIG),","+                                       \"%s has RestartSteps=%u, refusing to show more than %u steps.\",","+                                       rs->id, rs->restart_steps, RESTART_STEPS_MAX);","+","+        if (*printed && !sd_json_format_enabled(arg_json_format_flags))","+                putchar('\\n');","+        *printed = true;","+","+        if (never_restarted)","+                return show_never_restarted(rs, never_restarted);","+","+        table = table_new(\"restart\", \"delay\", \"total\");","+        if (!table)","+                return log_oom();","+","+        (void) table_set_align_percent(table, TABLE_HEADER_CELL(0), 100);","+        (void) table_set_align_percent(table, TABLE_HEADER_CELL(1), 100);","+        (void) table_set_align_percent(table, TABLE_HEADER_CELL(2), 100);","+","+        unsigned growth = restart_growth(rs);","+        usec_t further = restart_delay(rs, growth + 1);","+        hit = start_limit_hit(rs, &hit_usec);","+","+        for (unsigned n = 1; n <= growth && (hit == 0 || n <= hit); n++) {","+                usec_t d = restart_delay(rs, n);","+","+                total = usec_add(total, d);","+","+                r = table_add_many(","+                                table,","+                                TABLE_UINT, n,","+                                TABLE_TIMESPAN_MSEC, d,","+                                TABLE_TIMESPAN_MSEC, total);","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return table_log_add_error(r);","+","+                r = sd_json_variant_append_arraybo(","+                                &jrestarts,","+                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_UNSIGNED(\"restart\", n),","+                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_UNSIGNED(\"delayUSec\", d),","+                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_UNSIGNED(\"totalUSec\", total));","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return log_oom();","+        }","+","+        if (sd_json_format_enabled(arg_json_format_flags)) {","+                r = sd_json_buildo(","+                                &v,","+                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_STRING(\"unit\", rs->id),","+                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_VARIANT(\"restarts\", jrestarts),","+                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_UNSIGNED(\"furtherDelayUSec\", further),","+                                JSON_BUILD_PAIR_CONDITION_UNSIGNED(hit > 0, \"startLimitHitRestart\", hit),","+                                JSON_BUILD_PAIR_CONDITION_UNSIGNED(hit > 0, \"startLimitHitUSec\", hit_usec));","+                if (r < 0)","+                        return log_oom();","+","+                return sd_json_variant_dump(v, arg_json_format_flags, stdout, NULL);","+        }","+","+        r = table_print_with_pager(table, SD_JSON_FORMAT_OFF, arg_pager_flags, arg_legend);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        if (hit > growth)","+                printf(\"\\nEvery further restart waits %s.\", FORMAT_TIMESPAN(further, USEC_PER_MSEC));","+","+        if (hit > 0)","+                printf(\"%sThe start limit rejects restart %\" PRIu64 \", %s after the first start, and %s enters \"","+                       \"the failed state.\\n\",","+                       hit > growth ? \" \" : \"\\n\",","+                       hit,","+                       FORMAT_TIMESPAN(hit_usec, USEC_PER_MSEC),","+                       rs->id);","+        else","+                printf(\"\\nEvery further restart waits %s. The start limit never rejects a restart, so the service \"","+                       \"manager restarts %s indefinitely.\\n\",","+                       FORMAT_TIMESPAN(further, USEC_PER_MSEC),","+                       rs->id);","+","+        return 0;","+}","+","+static int map_restart_force_exit_status(","+                sd_bus *bus,","+                const char *member,","+                sd_bus_message *m,","+                sd_bus_error *error,","+                void *userdata) {","+","+        bool *forced = ASSERT_PTR(userdata);","+        const void *status, *signal;","+        size_t n_status, n_signal;","+        int r;","+","+        assert(m);","+","+        r = sd_bus_message_enter_container(m, 'r', \"aiai\");","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        r = sd_bus_message_read_array(m, 'i', &status, &n_status);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        r = sd_bus_message_read_array(m, 'i', &signal, &n_signal);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        r = sd_bus_message_exit_container(m);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return r;","+","+        *forced = n_status > 0 || n_signal > 0;","+        return 0;","+}","+","+static int restart_delays_online(sd_bus *bus, const char *arg, bool *printed) {","+        static const struct bus_properties_map map[] = {","+                { \"Id\",                     \"s\",      NULL,                          offsetof(RestartSettings, id)                        },","+                { \"LoadState\",              \"s\",      NULL,                          offsetof(RestartSettings, load_state)                },","+                { \"Restart\",                \"s\",      NULL,                          offsetof(RestartSettings, restart)                   },","+                { \"RestartForceExitStatus\", \"(aiai)\", map_restart_force_exit_status, offsetof(RestartSettings, restart_forced)            },","+                { \"RestartUSec\",            \"t\",      NULL,                          offsetof(RestartSettings, restart_usec)              },","+                { \"RestartSteps\",           \"u\",      NULL,                          offsetof(RestartSettings, restart_steps)             },","+                { \"RestartMaxDelayUSec\",    \"t\",      NULL,                          offsetof(RestartSettings, restart_max_delay_usec)    },","+                { \"StartLimitIntervalUSec\", \"t\",      NULL,                          offsetof(RestartSettings, start_limit_interval_usec) },","+                { \"StartLimitBurst\",        \"u\",      NULL,                          offsetof(RestartSettings, start_limit_burst)         },","+                {},","+        };","+        _cleanup_(sd_bus_error_free) sd_bus_error error = SD_BUS_ERROR_NULL;","+        _cleanup_(restart_settings_done) RestartSettings rs = {};","+        _cleanup_free_ char *unit = NULL, *path = NULL;","+        int r;","+","+        assert(bus);","+        assert(arg);","+        assert(printed);","+","+        r = unit_name_mangle_with_suffix(arg, NULL, UNIT_NAME_MANGLE_WARN, \".service\", &unit);","+        if (r < 0)","+                return log_error_errno(r, \"Failed to mangle name '%s': %m\", arg);","+","+        if (!endswith(unit, \".service\"))","+                return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EINVAL), \"Unit %s is not a serv